WEBVTT

00:00:06.083 --> 00:00:08.041
-<i>Good morning.</i>
-<i>Morning.</i>

00:00:12.041 --> 00:00:15.250
<i>Park Hyeong-seok.</i>

00:00:15.458 --> 00:00:20.250
<i>Tall frame, chiseled good looks,</i>
<i>and rich. He has it all. A true elite.</i>

00:00:20.458 --> 00:00:22.791
<i>He took down Lee Jin-seong</i>
<i>as soon as he got here.</i>

00:00:22.916 --> 00:00:25.375
<i>He's currently the hottest guy in school.</i>

00:00:26.041 --> 00:00:28.916
<i>To my shock and amazement,</i>
<i>he's even a good singer.</i>

00:00:29.916 --> 00:00:32.541
<i>And now, he's standing in my house.</i>

00:00:32.875 --> 00:00:36.125
Thanks for the invite.

00:00:36.958 --> 00:00:38.416
<i>This must be his first time</i>

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:40.333
<i>coming into a place as shabby as this.</i>

00:00:40.458 --> 00:00:42.458
<i>What if he's disappointed by me?</i>

00:00:43.291 --> 00:00:46.416
Oh, uh…
I… I'm so sorry.

00:00:46.916 --> 00:00:48.375
The… the place is pretty messy, huh?

00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:50.916
My grandma's really busy
with work, so…

00:00:51.041 --> 00:00:52.250
-Deok-hwa…
-Uh.

00:00:52.375 --> 00:00:54.750
…it's daytime.
Why do you have the lights on?

00:00:56.208 --> 00:00:57.208
Uh. Hmm?

00:00:57.333 --> 00:00:59.791
You need to save
on the electricity bill. And also…

00:01:00.458 --> 00:01:02.416
better to keep
the newspapers in a tidy stack.

00:01:02.541 --> 00:01:03.958
-Huh?
-If you put them

00:01:04.041 --> 00:01:07.250
between shoes or clothes,
it removes unwanted moisture.

00:01:09.333 --> 00:01:11.333
Oh, and they're good
for cleaning windows too.

00:01:11.833 --> 00:01:13.750
The oil in the ink absorbs all the dust.

00:01:14.666 --> 00:01:16.750
You must have had
a great upbringing to know all this.

00:01:16.875 --> 00:01:21.083
I guess I learned by watching
my mother do all this stuff at home.

00:01:21.166 --> 00:01:23.166
My grandmother brings home

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:24.916
these newspapers to do that too.

00:01:25.125 --> 00:01:27.958
Uh. She says you can make vegetables
last over a week if you store them

00:01:28.041 --> 00:01:29.583
rolled up in a newspaper.

00:01:29.875 --> 00:01:31.375
Oh, my mom does that too.

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:33.416
She says if the newspaper
is rolled up tight enough,

00:01:33.500 --> 00:01:35.083
it will keep the potatoes from sprouting.

00:01:35.208 --> 00:01:37.000
-Oh, sorry.
-Hmm?

00:01:37.125 --> 00:01:38.208
Sorry, I'm being rude.

00:01:38.416 --> 00:01:40.791
I'm not here to clean your place,
I… I came to practice.

00:01:40.875 --> 00:01:42.791
Oh, it's fine.

00:01:43.458 --> 00:01:44.416
Hmm.

00:01:44.833 --> 00:01:46.541
About practicing that song.

00:01:47.791 --> 00:01:50.916
-Do you really think I can sing it?
-Oh, of course you can!

00:01:51.916 --> 00:01:55.125
It's hard to express,
but when you sing, Hyeong-seok,

00:01:55.541 --> 00:01:58.333
it feels earnest.
And it makes me feel warm all over.

00:01:59.166 --> 00:02:01.250
And I'm confident
about my rapping.

00:02:01.583 --> 00:02:04.875
With your singing and my rapping,
we'll knock everyone off their feet.

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:06.916
Huh?

00:02:07.791 --> 00:02:09.916
Uh. I'd like you to listen to this.

00:02:17.083 --> 00:02:18.708
Huh? This is…

00:02:19.083 --> 00:02:21.166
I rearranged the song you sang.

00:02:21.750 --> 00:02:24.208
Uh. I like the melody.
What song is it from?

00:02:25.041 --> 00:02:28.583
Oh, I don't really know.
I can't remember where I heard it.

00:02:29.708 --> 00:02:32.916
-It just spilled out of me.
-Spilled out of you?

00:02:33.291 --> 00:02:34.625
Well, it's just--

00:02:35.083 --> 00:02:38.333
I think it's just something I sing
when I'm feeling blue and lonely.

00:02:39.041 --> 00:02:42.125
I think it might just be
my way of escaping reality.

00:02:42.458 --> 00:02:45.000
-Oh, the melody changed right there.
-Oh…

00:02:45.333 --> 00:02:48.125
The one you sang
was too short to sustain a full song.

00:02:48.375 --> 00:02:50.250
So, I added a new melody to fill it out.

00:02:50.333 --> 00:02:52.291
Wow, you're a composer too?

00:02:52.375 --> 00:02:57.291
-Oh, well, just a bit.
-That's amazing.

00:02:57.583 --> 00:03:00.125
This is
just a rough sketch, so it might suck.

00:03:02.541 --> 00:03:03.708
What do you think?

00:03:04.208 --> 00:03:06.208
Wow, it's great.

00:03:07.083 --> 00:03:08.500
You made it so much better.

00:03:08.875 --> 00:03:11.750
Oh, it'll get better
once it's mixed and mastered.

00:03:11.958 --> 00:03:15.208
Oh! And I'm going to try to make
the lyrics a little catchier if I can.

00:03:16.208 --> 00:03:19.208
<i>Whoa, so dedicated.</i>

00:03:20.125 --> 00:03:22.125
<i>He's truly incredible.</i>

00:05:01.916 --> 00:05:04.333
I'm sorry,
I couldn't practice for any longer.

00:05:04.458 --> 00:05:07.291
Oh, it's not your fault.
You have to go to work.

00:05:07.791 --> 00:05:10.458
Still, I was surprised
that you have a part-time job.

00:05:10.666 --> 00:05:13.375
It's only right for me.
Earn my money to live on.

00:05:13.541 --> 00:05:15.708
All right, then we can practice
at lunch time,

00:05:15.916 --> 00:05:18.000
-since you won't have time after school.
-Yeah.

00:05:20.875 --> 00:05:25.416
Oh, I'm so sorry. I should have
fixed you something to eat earlier.

00:05:25.750 --> 00:05:29.416
Oh, no, it's… it's fine. Thanks to you,
I got to listen to great music.

00:05:29.541 --> 00:05:31.416
Ah! Deok-hwa…

00:05:31.541 --> 00:05:33.208
-Uh.
-Oh…

00:05:33.791 --> 00:05:35.125
Oh!

00:05:35.250 --> 00:05:36.791
Is this your friend?

00:05:37.041 --> 00:05:38.833
So, this is your grandmother?

00:05:38.958 --> 00:05:40.083
Yeah.

00:05:40.958 --> 00:05:43.458
Hmm. Nice to meet you, ma'am.

00:05:43.666 --> 00:05:45.458
I'm Park Hyeong-seok, Deok-hwa's friend.

00:05:45.541 --> 00:05:46.958
Goodness!

00:05:47.125 --> 00:05:49.500
My grandson has so many friends.

00:05:50.208 --> 00:05:51.583
Oh, uh…

00:05:52.041 --> 00:05:53.000
TTEOKBOKKI, FISH CAKE, FRIES

00:05:53.083 --> 00:05:55.375
Uh. It's getting late.
Have something to eat before you go.

00:05:56.041 --> 00:05:57.208
Mm-hmm.

00:06:00.166 --> 00:06:02.083
Come on, don't be shy.

00:06:02.250 --> 00:06:04.083
Thank you

00:06:04.166 --> 00:06:05.416
for the offer, ma'am.

00:06:05.750 --> 00:06:08.083
It's just that I'm full.

00:06:08.541 --> 00:06:10.500
-Huh?
-Thank you for thinking of me.

00:06:10.833 --> 00:06:12.291
I know that you're busy working.

00:06:12.916 --> 00:06:15.250
Oh, I see.

00:06:15.583 --> 00:06:17.750
Goodbye, ma'am.

00:06:17.833 --> 00:06:20.291
See you later, Deok-hwa.

00:06:20.375 --> 00:06:21.291
Okay.

00:06:22.708 --> 00:06:26.000
-Oh, my. Nice young man.
-Hmm.

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:36.875
The song and the lyrics
are so fire.

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:38.208
Of course they are.

00:06:38.791 --> 00:06:43.166
I paid a hefty sum to a famous lyricist
and a composer to write it for me.

00:06:46.083 --> 00:06:48.791
It's only a high school festival though,
you know.

00:06:49.083 --> 00:06:50.916
You sure you don't mind us
singing this great song?

00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:53.125
The song is targeted at high school kids.

00:06:53.250 --> 00:06:57.083
It's a good opportunity to try
the song out and see how the kids respond.

00:06:57.708 --> 00:07:01.041
If we get a good response there,
we'll use it as your debut song.

00:07:01.166 --> 00:07:02.750
Are you serious?

00:07:02.958 --> 00:07:04.583
Absolutely.

00:07:04.666 --> 00:07:06.166
And if they like you too…

00:07:06.250 --> 00:07:07.708
-…I'll let you debut…
-Huh?

00:07:07.791 --> 00:07:08.833
…with Ho-bin.

00:07:08.958 --> 00:07:11.125
So, do your best.

00:07:11.333 --> 00:07:13.750
-I'll give it my all, sir!
-Okay, okay.

00:07:14.041 --> 00:07:17.083
If this goes well,
you'll be a part of this world.

00:07:17.458 --> 00:07:19.791
Do you have any idea
how good you can have it?

00:07:20.041 --> 00:07:24.041
Money, women or anything else you'd want,
is all yours for the taking.

00:07:35.458 --> 00:07:37.291
-I love this.
-Oh, wait, really?

00:07:37.458 --> 00:07:39.208
Yeah, this is so great.

00:07:39.416 --> 00:07:41.375
You wrote these lyrics in a day?

00:07:41.500 --> 00:07:42.833
You're incredible, Deok-hwa.

00:07:43.000 --> 00:07:46.666
I always jot down my thoughts
whenever I think of an idea for lyrics.

00:07:46.958 --> 00:07:49.583
-Should we start practicing, then?
-Yes.

00:07:59.458 --> 00:08:01.083
Amazing!

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:04.125
Man, I am shook!

00:08:04.416 --> 00:08:07.541
Honestly, I thought you'd have trouble
connecting to this song.

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:09.250
-Oh…
-On account of how we live

00:08:09.333 --> 00:08:10.583
in such different worlds.

00:08:11.208 --> 00:08:12.208
Hmm.

00:08:12.625 --> 00:08:14.291
But, I don't know how to put this…

00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:17.625
I felt your sincerity through the song.

00:08:18.750 --> 00:08:20.708
-Well, thank you.
-But if I can be…

00:08:20.833 --> 00:08:22.291
-Huh?
-…real here,

00:08:22.583 --> 00:08:25.291
there's no denying you're expressive,
but your technique needs more work.

00:08:25.375 --> 00:08:27.375
-Oh…
-We only have two weeks left

00:08:27.458 --> 00:08:29.041
-until the festival.
-Hmm.

00:08:29.125 --> 00:08:31.541
Not much time
and you won't get better right away,

00:08:31.666 --> 00:08:32.916
even with practice.

00:08:33.083 --> 00:08:35.458
-Then… what should I do about it?
-Hmm.

00:08:36.875 --> 00:08:40.708
It won't be perfect,
but just focus on memorizing the song,

00:08:40.916 --> 00:08:43.291
rather than
on vocalizing or on breathing.

00:08:43.833 --> 00:08:47.625
Don't overwork your vocal cords.
We don't want to do any damage to them.

00:08:47.750 --> 00:08:51.458
Right. I can probably spare
about an hour and a half after school too.

00:08:51.625 --> 00:08:55.666
Yeah, then we can dedicate
that time and lunches to our practice.

00:08:55.833 --> 00:08:57.000
Yeah.

00:09:02.208 --> 00:09:04.625
Hey, are you okay?

00:09:05.166 --> 00:09:06.541
My throat's a little sore.

00:09:07.500 --> 00:09:09.833
-It is?
-And I didn't even sing all that much.

00:09:09.958 --> 00:09:11.625
Vocal cords are delicate.

00:09:12.125 --> 00:09:15.375
Careful, so your voice doesn't get hoarse.
And don't overdo it with practicing.

00:09:15.750 --> 00:09:18.583
I'll keep that in mind.

00:09:23.833 --> 00:09:25.708
Flight
You can cry, let it all out if you want

00:09:30.500 --> 00:09:33.041
<i>I just want to be friends.</i>

00:09:33.875 --> 00:09:35.750
<i>Why… with someone like me?</i>

00:09:36.750 --> 00:09:39.416
<i>I don't know.</i>
<i>Because you're like me.</i>

00:09:43.208 --> 00:09:45.041
<i>Is it my fault that we're poor?</i>

00:09:47.041 --> 00:09:48.791
<i>Wow, you're a composer too?</i>

00:09:48.875 --> 00:09:51.250
Oh, well just a bit.

00:09:51.500 --> 00:09:53.416
<i>That's amazing.</i>

00:09:55.416 --> 00:09:57.666
<i>He's not like me at all. </i>

00:09:58.208 --> 00:10:01.333
<i>Right now, all I can do is…</i>

00:10:16.416 --> 00:10:18.375
24+ CONVENIENCE STORE

00:10:27.500 --> 00:10:30.666
Huh? Oh, my throat.
It doesn't hurt at all.

00:10:31.208 --> 00:10:34.916
Oh, yeah that's right.
Because I wasn't practicing in this body.

00:10:47.291 --> 00:10:48.750
Huh?

00:10:49.375 --> 00:10:52.916
-Uh.
-Giving your voice a workout today?

00:10:53.000 --> 00:10:54.333
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:10:54.458 --> 00:10:55.958
I didn't know you were here.

00:10:56.166 --> 00:10:58.625
You have a really nice voice.

00:11:01.083 --> 00:11:02.208
THROAT LOZENGE

00:11:02.333 --> 00:11:03.875
Have these when you practice.

00:11:04.041 --> 00:11:06.291
-Huh?
-They're good for your throat.

00:11:06.541 --> 00:11:09.458
Oh, uh, thank you, miss.
You've been really--

00:11:09.625 --> 00:11:11.208
I mean, that's nice of you.

00:11:12.166 --> 00:11:15.333
Good luck. Happy singing!

00:11:17.375 --> 00:11:18.666
Oh…

00:11:30.041 --> 00:11:31.458
-Oh, Hyeong-seok…
-Huh?

00:11:31.541 --> 00:11:33.208
…you shouldn't be doing that.

00:11:33.291 --> 00:11:35.416
Oh, am I not supposed
to sing it like this?

00:11:35.500 --> 00:11:36.708
Didn't I tell you?

00:11:36.791 --> 00:11:40.125
Vocal cords are delicate, so really,
you shouldn't practice too much.

00:11:40.291 --> 00:11:43.041
Oh, no! I… I didn't practice it at all.

00:11:44.166 --> 00:11:45.750
Uh. Really?

00:11:46.250 --> 00:11:47.291
Yeah.

00:11:47.375 --> 00:11:49.416
<i>Not in this body anyway.</i>

00:11:49.625 --> 00:11:52.083
Truthfully, Hyeong-seok…

00:11:53.208 --> 00:11:54.916
you, uh…

00:11:55.208 --> 00:11:59.250
you must be a genius. I can't believe
how much better you've gotten in two days!

00:11:59.708 --> 00:12:02.750
-A genius? No, no way.
-All right then,

00:12:02.958 --> 00:12:05.083
let's try something different
in the intro.

00:12:07.041 --> 00:12:09.416
-Try improvising with the song like that.
-Okay.

00:12:09.958 --> 00:12:12.458
Wow, Hyeong-seok's so amazing.

00:12:20.958 --> 00:12:23.125
Hyeong-seok shines
at whatever he's doing.

00:12:23.666 --> 00:12:25.875
-Hey.
-Uh…

00:12:26.083 --> 00:12:28.666
I heard you're performing
with that good-looking transfer student

00:12:28.750 --> 00:12:30.000
in the festival.

00:12:30.500 --> 00:12:32.250
Oh, what about it?

00:12:33.041 --> 00:12:35.250
What? "What about it?"

00:12:35.750 --> 00:12:38.416
Nah…

00:12:45.583 --> 00:12:46.666
Man…

00:12:46.750 --> 00:12:48.708
…thinking for yourself now?

00:12:48.791 --> 00:12:51.750
So, you're going to piggyback
on the transfer student's popularity?

00:12:51.833 --> 00:12:53.125
The pig's using

00:12:53.208 --> 00:12:55.208
-his brain, huh?
-Yeah. Look at him,

00:12:55.333 --> 00:12:56.708
he's got all kinds of plans.

00:12:56.791 --> 00:12:58.666
I'm for it
if Park Hyeong-seok's

00:12:58.750 --> 00:12:59.958
the only one on stage.

00:13:03.500 --> 00:13:04.416
Hey!

00:13:04.541 --> 00:13:06.041
You hit him too.

00:13:07.875 --> 00:13:09.625
Go over there and hit him too!

00:13:14.708 --> 00:13:15.708
Hey…

00:13:15.791 --> 00:13:18.041
…if you don't do it,
we'll beat you up twice as hard.

00:13:32.583 --> 00:13:34.208
Huh?

00:13:34.541 --> 00:13:37.041
Yeah, I… I'm on my way.
I'll be there soon.

00:13:38.583 --> 00:13:42.041
I have to go get my vocal lesson,
so I'll let you off the hook for today.

00:13:42.583 --> 00:13:43.541
You fat-ass.

00:13:43.666 --> 00:13:46.166
We should have beaten him more
so he could squeal.

00:13:50.166 --> 00:13:54.500
Sorry.

00:13:55.333 --> 00:13:56.375
Huh?

00:13:56.916 --> 00:13:59.958
-Why would you… be sorry?
-I…

00:14:01.500 --> 00:14:05.375
I'm such a scumbag!

00:14:06.250 --> 00:14:08.666
Huh?

00:14:16.791 --> 00:14:19.375
Uh. Welcome to our store. Oh.

00:14:19.541 --> 00:14:21.000
Oh…

00:14:21.125 --> 00:14:23.000
Hmm.

00:14:26.500 --> 00:14:29.291
Hey, guys.
What are you two doing here together?

00:14:30.708 --> 00:14:31.875
Hey, uh…

00:14:32.875 --> 00:14:36.083
-I'm Pyeon Deok-hwa, nice to meet you.
-Huh?

00:14:36.166 --> 00:14:39.708
<i>Oh, oh, right. This is the first</i>
<i>time I'm meeting him in this body.</i>

00:14:39.916 --> 00:14:43.750
He's got something
he really needs to talk to you about.

00:14:44.000 --> 00:14:46.250
Hmm? What's the matter?

00:14:49.625 --> 00:14:50.750
Um.

00:14:51.041 --> 00:14:55.000
The truth is, I didn't have
the courage to come on my own,

00:14:55.833 --> 00:14:58.041
so I asked him to come with me.

00:14:59.333 --> 00:15:00.833
Oh, I see.

00:15:01.458 --> 00:15:03.125
You know, those guys who…

00:15:03.250 --> 00:15:05.333
…got me to steal the charger
and to hit you.

00:15:05.708 --> 00:15:08.041
Well, those guys go to my school too.

00:15:08.583 --> 00:15:10.250
Oh, yeah, I knew that.

00:15:10.833 --> 00:15:13.083
We have a lot of bullies at school

00:15:13.708 --> 00:15:16.750
and they've been tormenting me
for as long as I can remember.

00:15:18.458 --> 00:15:21.541
I know it's no excuse
for me hitting you, though.

00:15:21.958 --> 00:15:23.833
No, really, it's okay.

00:15:24.333 --> 00:15:28.208
They made you do it after all.
You don't have to apologize for that.

00:15:29.208 --> 00:15:32.833
This is not
what I came to high school for.

00:15:33.291 --> 00:15:36.208
I like clothes.
Shirts and belts and shoes…

00:15:36.375 --> 00:15:39.958
That's why I came to this school,
to learn everything about fashion.

00:15:40.041 --> 00:15:41.416
Me too.

00:15:42.333 --> 00:15:44.500
I came because music is in my soul.

00:15:53.750 --> 00:15:54.958
Me too.

00:15:55.166 --> 00:15:58.916
I used to be bullied really badly
at the school I used to go to.

00:15:59.083 --> 00:16:02.291
-Uh. Wait, you're in what year?
-I'm the same age as you guys.

00:16:02.458 --> 00:16:04.250
-Freshman.
-Wait, you are?

00:16:04.583 --> 00:16:06.291
So, you don't have to be

00:16:06.375 --> 00:16:07.625
too formal with me.

00:16:07.708 --> 00:16:09.541
I've been through so much too.

00:16:09.833 --> 00:16:13.041
I've been beaten to a pulp
and had my face dunked in the toilet.

00:16:13.125 --> 00:16:14.458
Huh? Me too!

00:16:14.750 --> 00:16:16.791
There was one time
I had to do a naked somersault.

00:16:17.000 --> 00:16:18.666
I was a human fan once.

00:16:18.833 --> 00:16:20.750
I rolled around on the bathroom floor.

00:16:20.958 --> 00:16:21.916
I licked a shoe.

00:16:22.000 --> 00:16:24.791
-I was a human punching bag.
-I got beat up in front of my mom.

00:16:28.375 --> 00:16:30.041
Oh, jeez!

00:16:30.166 --> 00:16:31.625
I can't believe they did that.

00:16:33.250 --> 00:16:36.166
Ever since,
Hyeong-seok transferred in though,

00:16:36.875 --> 00:16:39.750
-it's gotten a lot better.
-Oh, yeah, that's right.

00:16:40.208 --> 00:16:43.333
Hyeong-seok is this really good-looking
transfer student…

00:16:43.416 --> 00:16:44.625
-Hmm.
-…and I thought

00:16:44.708 --> 00:16:47.416
-he was just like the other guys at first.
-Hmm.

00:16:47.666 --> 00:16:51.166
But thanks to him,
Jin-seong's stopped bullying me entirely.

00:16:52.291 --> 00:16:55.666
Oh, Jin-seong's one of the guys
who used to bully me all the time.

00:16:55.791 --> 00:16:58.166
When Hyeong-seok was nice to me,

00:16:58.916 --> 00:17:01.666
I first thought it was because he wanted
to use me in some way.

00:17:02.125 --> 00:17:03.208
That wasn't it.

00:17:03.666 --> 00:17:06.250
He's miles better than me,
in both looks and character,

00:17:07.250 --> 00:17:08.458
<i>but he said I was like him.</i>

00:17:09.458 --> 00:17:11.333
<i>And this might be embarrassing,</i>

00:17:11.708 --> 00:17:14.125
but Hyeong-seok
is kind of like me, I feel it.

00:17:14.625 --> 00:17:16.083
Just like the said to me.

00:17:16.458 --> 00:17:19.708
I think that is why Hyeong-seok
can sing my song,

00:17:19.833 --> 00:17:20.958
my lyrics, with such soul.

00:17:21.500 --> 00:17:23.666
-He gets it.
-Wow…

00:17:24.416 --> 00:17:25.375
Thank you.

00:17:25.541 --> 00:17:26.583
-Hmm?
-Uh?

00:17:26.666 --> 00:17:28.708
-Why'd you say thank you to that?
-Huh?

00:17:28.875 --> 00:17:31.125
-Uh. Um. I mean, um…
-Is that true?

00:17:31.208 --> 00:17:32.500
Huh?

00:17:34.333 --> 00:17:35.458
What you just said.

00:17:35.666 --> 00:17:37.291
-Is that the truth?
-Uh…

00:17:37.708 --> 00:17:40.541
-Basco…
-Thank you so much for helping me before.

00:17:40.750 --> 00:17:42.416
I'm asking you straight out.

00:17:43.083 --> 00:17:46.000
The transfer student
is a good guy in your opinion?

00:17:46.208 --> 00:17:49.208
-Yeah, I'm sure of it.
-Yeah, yeah, it's true.

00:17:49.333 --> 00:17:53.125
He always asks me to eat lunch with him,
and he never really asks me for anything.

00:17:53.291 --> 00:17:55.291
But I caught him red handed
taking your mother's money.

00:17:55.500 --> 00:17:58.125
Huh? My mother's money?

00:17:59.041 --> 00:18:02.875
Oh, you saw that? Oh, wait, no.

00:18:03.000 --> 00:18:05.333
My mother gave him that
to pay for the coffee.

00:18:05.583 --> 00:18:09.000
-Is that right?
-Yes, really. I swear, it's all true.

00:18:10.916 --> 00:18:14.500
Convenience store boy,
I thank you.

00:18:15.291 --> 00:18:16.791
-Uh.
-I was mistaken about him.

00:18:17.416 --> 00:18:21.333
And also, you can always call on me,
if you need to train.

00:18:23.666 --> 00:18:24.791
Whoa…

00:18:34.750 --> 00:18:36.750
Here, I'll play it.

00:18:37.125 --> 00:18:38.000
Okay.

00:18:46.208 --> 00:18:48.375
-Mm-hmm.
-Hmm.

00:19:47.083 --> 00:19:50.208
Oh, the rearrangement is so good.

00:19:51.291 --> 00:19:52.416
What is it?

00:19:52.833 --> 00:19:54.875
I can't believe how good you've gotten,

00:19:55.791 --> 00:19:57.291
in just the last ten days!

00:19:57.458 --> 00:19:59.500
You think so?

00:19:59.625 --> 00:20:01.625
You're a genius, I knew it.

00:20:02.083 --> 00:20:05.083
<i>Well, I've been practicing 24/7</i>
<i>in both bodies.</i>

00:20:05.416 --> 00:20:06.958
-Everyone…
-Hmm?

00:20:07.041 --> 00:20:11.416
…is going to be so surprised by this!
I revised some of my lyrics

00:20:11.541 --> 00:20:12.708
for the rap.

00:20:14.916 --> 00:20:17.750
This is great. It's perfect, Deok-hwa.

00:20:18.541 --> 00:20:21.000
With your singing and my rapping…

00:20:21.125 --> 00:20:22.583
…we're invincible!

00:20:33.708 --> 00:20:36.833
-What do you think?
-Hmm. It's not bad.

00:20:38.125 --> 00:20:39.875
-I can smell it.
-Huh? Huh?

00:20:39.958 --> 00:20:41.458
The smell of a big hit.

00:20:41.583 --> 00:20:43.375
-You think so?
-Yeah.

00:20:44.583 --> 00:20:48.541
I know this world like
the back of my hand, trust me.

00:20:51.666 --> 00:20:54.875
Hmm. What should
the cover of our first album be?

00:20:55.333 --> 00:20:57.791
I don't know,
maybe something like Zico, huh?

00:20:58.000 --> 00:20:59.833
They have the performance list
for the festival.

00:21:00.041 --> 00:21:02.291
-When do we perform?
-Second to last.

00:21:02.375 --> 00:21:04.541
Ugh! We should be the last.
We're a headline act.

00:21:04.750 --> 00:21:07.500
No way, it's all good.

00:21:07.708 --> 00:21:09.083
-The pig and the transfer student…
-Huh?

00:21:09.166 --> 00:21:10.416
…are going last.

00:21:10.500 --> 00:21:12.500
It's obvious they're just trying
to get to attention using…

00:21:12.583 --> 00:21:14.041
20 - PARK HYEONG-SEOK,
PYEON DEOK-HWA

00:21:14.125 --> 00:21:15.625
…that idiot, Park Hyeong-seok's face.

00:21:15.708 --> 00:21:17.458
I bet they see
our performance,

00:21:17.583 --> 00:21:19.083
get intimidated, and bolt.

00:21:19.291 --> 00:21:21.750
And besides,
it's the Pig's first performance.

00:21:22.375 --> 00:21:28.250
It's time I put these guys down.
